<title>UK: Reuters' 56th ex-UK air cargo market report.</title>
<headline>Reuters' 56th ex-UK air cargo market report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current average ex-UK GBP air cargo market rates per kg for a 100 kg shipment, with a volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-one. Rates are exclusive of cargo fuel surcharges being applied by airlines.</p>
<p>			    Nov 29    vs    Nov 13</p>
<p>			   UNITED STATES</p>
<p>  LON-JFK		 0.63		O.63</p>
<p>  LON-LAX		 0.73		0.73</p>
<p>  LON-CHI		 0.74		0.74</p>
<p>			   ASIA-PACIFIC</p>
<p>  LON-HKG		 1.22	    1.21</p>
<p>  LON-SIN		 1.29	    1.28</p>
<p>  LON-NRT		 2.05	    2.04</p>
<p>  LON-SEL		 2.00	    1.99</p>
<p>  LON-SYD		 2.17	    2.15</p>
<p>			   MIDDLE EAST</p>
<p>  LON-DXB		 0.87	    0.88</p>
<p>  LON-BAH		 0.95	    0.95</p>
<p>			   AFRICA</p>
<p>  LON-JNB		 1.80	    1.80</p>
<p>			   SCANDINAVIA</p>
<p>  LON-STO		 0.74	    0.73</p>
<p>  LON-CPH		 0.70	    0.69</p>
<p>			   LATIN AMERICA</p>
<p>  LON-SAO		 2.XX	    2.06</p>
<p>  LON-BUE		 2.XX	    2.25</p>
<p>*The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters journalists on confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents based at the three main London airports.</p>
<p>*All prices quoted in sterling.</p>
<p>*The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices and are indicative or current market activity. Ex-UK air cargo rates steady to firm on high volume -- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017 No text received</p>
